course: dictionary
lesson: 11318
title: Legends and evidence
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A yeti is a large, hairy, ape-like creature that some people say lives high in the Himalaya mountains. Nobody has ever proved it is real, so it is a legend, a story people tell that may not be true. The clues in the sentence tell you this: «It is a legend, and no one has ever proved it is real.»
explain: Context helps you work out what unknown words mean. «There is no good evidence it lives on as a Yeti or Bigfoot.» The words no good evidence tell you that nothing solid backs up the claim. Evidence means facts or proof that show something is true.
explain: Scientists check claims by looking for evidence. Footprints and hairs once said to be from a yeti turned out to be from bears and other animals. So a claim without good evidence is not proved, however exciting the story sounds.
fact: A yeti is a large, hairy, ape-like creature from legend.
fact: The yeti is also called the Abominable Snowman.
fact: Some people say the yeti lives in the Himalaya mountains, but no one has proved it.
fact: «Legend» means a story passed down from people long ago, which may not be true.
fact: «Evidence» means facts or proof that show something is true.
exercise: In «It is a legend, and no one has ever proved it is real», what does legend mean? | A true story that has been checked by scientists | *A story that may not be true | A map of the mountains | A kind of snow
exercise: What does «no good evidence» mean in «There is no good evidence it lives on as a Yeti»? | It is hidden in a cave | It is a very good idea | Lots of photographs prove it | *Nothing solid proves it
exercise: Why is the yeti called a claim without good evidence? | Scientists photographed one in the snow | Everyone in the world has seen one | *Its footprints and hairs turned out to be from bears and other animals | It is in every museum
test: What is another name for the yeti? | Mountain goat | Snow leopard | Himalaya | *Abominable Snowman
test: Which fact shows that a yeti claim is not proved? | It is a large, hairy creature | *Nobody has ever proved it is real | Some people say it lives in the Himalaya | It is also called the Abominable Snowman
exam: In «Gigantopithecus died out a few hundred thousand years ago», what does died out mean? | Grew very large | *Stopped existing, with none left alive | Moved up the mountains | Got lost in the forest
